<ContentPage title="Retreat Center" subtitle="Where ancient wisdom meets modern practice.">
  <p>
    The Technoshamanic Retreat Center is BARK's cultural and healing heart. A space where technology and
    tradition aren't opposites but partners — where meditation meets neuroscience, where plant medicine
    meets pharmacology, where ancestral wisdom meets open inquiry.
  </p>

  <h2>What Happens Here</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Retreats</strong> — structured programs blending contemplative practices, nature immersion, and technology detox/integration</li>
    <li><strong>Healing</strong> — holistic wellness drawing on both indigenous Yungas traditions and evidence-based modern approaches</li>
    <li><strong>Culture</strong> — arts, music, storytelling, ceremony — the things that make a community more than a collection of buildings</li>
    <li><strong>Research</strong> — careful, respectful study of consciousness, altered states, and the intersection of technology and the human spirit</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Technoshamanism</h2>
  <p>
    We use this term deliberately. "Techno" because we embrace technology as a tool for human flourishing.
    "Shamanic" because we respect that not everything that matters can be measured, and that the deepest
    human knowledge often comes through direct experience rather than abstraction.
  </p>
  <p>
    This isn't New Age escapism. It's a rigorous, open-minded exploration of what it means to be human
    in an age of accelerating technological change.
  </p>

  <h2>Revenue and Sustainability</h2>
  <p>
    The Retreat Center is also a key revenue source for BARK. International visitors pay for retreat programs,
    which funds community operations and local employment. This creates a virtuous cycle: the more attractive
    the community and its setting, the more sustainable it becomes.
  </p>

